# LF in every checkout, Windows included. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which checks out CRLF: bash then reads
# `set -euo pipefail\r` and every script, hook and shell template here
# breaks — scripts/validate.sh first, which is the Windows test path.
# PowerShell and provision read LF fine, so there is no file that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
